X: 1
T: Adiós Muchachos
C: Julio César Sanders (music), César Vedani (lyrics), 1927
O: Argentina
R: Tango
N: "Goodbye, boys": a dying man takes leave of his friends. Recorded by
N: Carlos Gardel in 1928 and one of the most widely played tangos since.
N: Melody and chords from mu-tech.org (WorldTrad/Adios_muchachos): the
N: arrangement MIDI and the printed lead sheet agree; this ABC renders back
N: to the arrangement's melody exactly (after transposition). In bar 12 the lead
N: sheet prints c-e-G; both of mu-tech's MIDIs play c-c-G, used here.
N: mu-tech's plain melody MIDI plays the eighths with a shuffle; the lead sheet
N: writes them straight, as here.
N: Transposed up a fourth from C to F to fit the recorder (range E4 to A5);
N: in C the tune dips to B3.
N: The accompaniment uses a tango 3-3-2 pattern (%%MIDI gchord).
